BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Potluck of Stories: Windham County Remembers
DTSTART:20261025T190000
DTEND:20261026T160000
DTSTAMP:20261025T145849Z
UID:3a7abc76be049ade5bb63124b972c3@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In honor of our nation's 250th\, the Historical Society of Win
 dham County (HSWC) presents A Potluck of Stories: Windham County Remembers
 . The weekend of stories from Windham County's past and present is Saturda
 y\, Oct. 24\, at 7 pm and Sunday\, Oct. 25\, at 2 pm at Newfane's Union Ha
 ll. The HSWC issued invitations to all 23 county towns for stories and tel
 lers: the resulting lineup represents many of those communities\; towns no
 t represented in stories will be acknowledged at some point over the cours
 e of the two-part program through interlocking patter. A different program
  for each date will include real-time stories told by residents of our tow
 ns: stories that shed a light on where we've come from to become who we ar
 e. Saturday’s lineup at 7PM includes Barbara Coleman\, Carleen Pelsue\, 
 Charlie Marchant\, Dane Rank\, David Parker\, Janet Lucier\, Jon Julian\, 
 Kent Young\, Leslie Zucker\, Marty Gehring\, Peter Erickson\, Susan Persa
 \, and Tino Benson. On the Sunday 2PM program will be Alan Bills\, Alex Lo
 ckie\, Bucky Pelsue\, Charlie Marchant\, Eli Galbraith\, Fred Homer\, Jean
  Allbee\, Mary McCoy\, Melanie Keiser\, Michael Bosworth\, Naima Wade\, Ri
 chard Wizansky\, Roger Allbee\, Rick Zamore\, and Steve Benson. The progra
 ms are free\, though donations to the Historical Society of Windham County
  will be welcomed. Union Hall is at 5 Church St.\, Newfane\, just off Rte.
  30.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Union Hall\, 5 Church St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/a-potluck-
 of-stories-windham-county-remembers-15-10-2026-19-25-22
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Fall Blacksmithing Workshop
DTSTART:20261025T100000
DTEND:20261025T150000
DTSTAMP:20261025T145849Z
UID:60a21ba0ad8cb818cffce2a3bbdd42@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to learn how to work with fire and shape 
 metal? In this one-day class for adult beginners\, participants will learn
  how to start and manage a fire\, ensure safe blacksmithing practices\, an
 d develop basic techniques for shaping metal including forming a hook\, tw
 isting\, and drifting. At the end of the class\, you will take home a hook
  or bracelet that you’ve made with your new skills! This is a 6-hour pro
 gram with workshop slots available on October 25 and November 14. The cost
  covers the class fee as well as materials. Attendees should bring a lunch
  and plenty of water. Aprons\, gloves\, and ear and eye protection will be
  provided. If you already own protective equipment you would like to use\,
  you are welcome to bring it to class to wear at the discretion of the ins
 tructor. Please wear natural fibers\, long pants\, and sturdy closed-toed 
 shoes such as boots. This class will involve repetitive motions and physic
 al activity with heavy items such as hammers\, and there will be breaks fo
 r all participants throughout. For accessibility questions\, please contac
 t us at info@lcmm.org or 802-475-2022.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Champlain Maritime Museum\, 4472 Basin Harbor Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/adult-fall
 -blacksmithing-workshop-28-08-2026-14-10-25
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Burlington Halloween Roll & Stroll
DTSTART:20261025T133000
DTEND:20261025T153000
DTSTAMP:20261025T145849Z
UID:91cb3694e4356bd4b3f78e984659ad@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join hundreds of costumed neighbors on a joyful\, fun-filled\,
  and not at all scary bike\, walk\, and roll on the streets of Burlington!
  Sunday\, October 25th. Please RSVP (not required\, but really helps with 
 planning): http://sevendaystickets.com/e/halloween-roll-stroll-2026 Ride t
 ogether throughout town\, culminating at Old Spokes Home for photos\, musi
 c\, and more. A great way to get more mileage out of your awesome costume 
 and have a blast with your community too. Please note\, motor vehicles (in
 cluding e-motos) are not permitted. All are welcome to join us on bicycles
 \, e-bikes\, trikes\, recumbents\, walkers\, strollers\, rollers\, etc. Br
 ought to you by Local Motion\, Old Spokes Home\, Vermont Clean Communities
 \, Peace & Justice Center\, Burlington Parks\, Recreation & Waterfront\, S
 even Days\, Walk to Shop\, and The Burlington Walk/Bike Council.\n\nSource
 s: Vermont Public
LOCATION:City Hall Park\, 135 Church St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/burlington
 -halloween-roll-stroll-09-10-2026-15-25-42
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween Kids Party
DTSTART:20261025T140000
DTEND:20261025T160000
DTSTAMP:20261025T145849Z
UID:2c43aa2ccf8f45ba4410d55ab829d1@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Our annual Halloween Kids Party is approaching! We will have a
  pumpkin carving station with enough pumpkins to share\, along with snacks
 \, games\, spooky stories\, and more! Meet the Mad Scientist Doctor Hearts
 on\, the master of playing spooky tunes. Kids will have the chance to sing
  and dance along to classic Halloween favorites like Monster Mash! Admissi
 on by Donation 🧡 Bring your little ghosts and goblins\, dress up in you
 r favorite costume\, and join us for a spooktacular afternoon! We can't wa
 it to celebrate Halloween with our community! 🎃👻 Parking at the Acad
 emy (across the street) 37 Academy Lane McIndoe Falls\, VT 05050 McIndoes 
 Academy Event Center\n\nSources: Vermont Public
